# One line ending, decided here rather than by whichever machine last touched a
# file. Without this, every commit made on Windows reports a hundred "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warnings and, worse, a file round-tripped through a
# different checkout shows as entirely rewritten in the diff.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: normalise to LF in the repository, and check out LF
# on every platform. Modern Windows tooling — VS Code, PowerShell, Next, Node —
# all handle LF perfectly well, so there is nothing to gain from CRLF locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must not touch them at all.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
